        "literature_status": "extends_known_mechanism",
        "summary": "Cacna1g loss produced a multi-gene FDR-significant response concentrated in 151 TH Prkcd Grin2c Glut.",
        "why_it_matters": "The result places the strongest transcriptional consequence of Cav3.1 loss in a thalamic glutamatergic population, matching the known thalamic dependence on Cav3.1 but extending it from excitability to a measured gene-expression state.",
        "genes": "Cacna1g|Ptprn|Stmn4|Cpne7|Ly6e|Zdhhc22|Jun|Iyd|Lrrc7|Serpine2|Notum|Irag1",
