        "literature_status": "refines_known_mechanism",
        "summary": "Cacna1c, Cacna1g, Cacna2d1, and Cacnb4 were knocked down in the same thalamic class but produced orthogonal transcriptomes, with Cacna1g giving a multi-gene response and Cacna1c/Cacna2d1/Cacnb4 mainly giving self-only signatures.",
        "why_it_matters": "Voltage-gated calcium-channel membership or auxiliary-subunit proximity is not enough to predict a shared scRNA-seq perturbation signature.",
        "genes": "Cacna1c|Cacna1g|Cacna2d1|Cacnb4|Ptprn|Stmn4|Cpne7",
